##C --> CA means insertion of "A" -- These are common in RNA-seq eQTL datasets because indels can be genotyped and tested alongside SNPs.

SNP	The specific genetic variant being tested for association with gene expression.
Chr	Chromosome of the SNP	
BP	Base-pair coordinate | Genomic position (typically in hg19/GRCh37).
A1	Effect allele, The allele whose dosage (0, 1, 2 copies) is used in the regression; the slope (b) refers to this allele.
A2	Non-effect allele, The other allele at the same locus. May represent the reference or the alternate allele; not necessarily minor.
Freq	Frequency of A1: Proportion of samples carrying the A1 allele. Values < 0.5 = A1 is minor; > 0.5 = A1 is major.
Probe	Expression feature ID: The tested RNA-seq feature (Ensembl gene or transcript ID). Called “probe” for historical consistency with microarray eQTLs.
Probe_Chr	Chromosome of the probe (gene)	
Probe_bp	Gene start coordinate: Approximate start (TSS) position of the gene or transcript.
Gene	Gene symbol: Readable HGNC symbol mapped to the Ensembl ID (e.g., TUBB8).
Orientation	Strand of the gene: “+” = forward strand; “–” = reverse strand.
b	Effect size (slope):	Change in normalized expression per additional A1 allele. Positive = A1 increases expression; negative = A1 decreases expression.
SE	Standard error of b:	Sampling uncertainty of the effect estimate.
p	Nominal p-value: Statistical significance for association between genotype dosage and expression.

