# Idea — “take eQTLs detected in other datasets and then contrast effect sizes estimated from your two groups” 
#is an approach for reducing winner’s curse / discovery bias.

# In other words: Don’t do discovery vs replication (where you test significance twice).

# Instead, define a fixed set of SNP–gene pairs (e.g., all known cis-eQTLs from BrainMeta),
# and then compare estimated betas (b) across your two conditions.

# This is often called an effect-size concordance or context-dependent eQTL (CD-eQTL) analysis.

